{
 "sub_strand": "MATH.G9.MEASUR.MONEY",
 "title": "Money",
 "status": "draft: written 18 Nov 2026 offline for Grade 9; not yet checked by a Kenyan maths teacher; not loaded by the live tutor",
 "sources": [],
 "notes": "Official outcomes a to e are tested; f (appreciate) is not a question. Currencies of other countries (a), changing money at a bureau with buying and selling rates, through a third currency, and reading a rate from a graph (b), import duty (c), excise duty, including duty per litre and working back to the factory price (d), and VAT at 16%, including the price before VAT (e). The rates in the families are for practice ('in this question'), not today's rates. Identifying currencies (a) has no family. Teacher to confirm: that Grade 9 learners work with the layered order import duty, then excise on value plus duty, then VAT on everything, as three families do; and the 16% VAT rate.",
 "skills": [
  {
   "skill": "MATH.G9.MEASUR.MONEY.CURRENCIES_IDENTIFY",
